WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.716 --> 00:00:10.360
Every teaching week has a short audio lecture. Your professor wrote each one; a disclosed AI narrator reads it for clarity and accessibility.

2
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:19.017
Press play on any week. The lecture keeps playing while you move around the site, so you can listen while you read or review.

3
00:00:19.017 --> 00:00:27.925
Use the mini player. While a lecture plays, a small player stays on screen. It can pause, jump you to that week's page, or close.

4
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:38.930
Open the week for the full player. The week page adds skip, speed, download, a follow-along transcript, and other narration voices and languages. Download before you travel; the subway has no signal.

5
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:49.933
Treat it as a companion, not a substitute. The lecture explains how the week fits together. The readings still carry the citations and evidence your graded work needs.

6
00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:53.132
Listening is never tracked or graded.

7
00:00:53.132 --> 00:00:58.438
Where next: Open the week the lecture belongs to and work its readings.
